{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00390",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.07,
      "end_seconds": 2.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Morning! Make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.44,
      "end_seconds": 6.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. It's been a long few days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.07,
      "end_seconds": 12.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.1,
      "end_seconds": 19.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome. Did you find the place alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.78,
      "end_seconds": 24.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Yes, it was easy enough. The parking was the hard part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.44,
      "end_seconds": 29.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Go ahead, tell me what's happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 30.45,
      "end_seconds": 33.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "We came because of occasional chest tightness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.44,
      "end_seconds": 39.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.14,
      "end_seconds": 43.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "It's been nearly five years, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.21,
      "end_seconds": 53.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.45,
      "end_seconds": 60.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "I'd say every other day. Yes, walking uphill. That makes it worse. It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.44,
      "end_seconds": 63.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.72,
      "end_seconds": 70.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "It usually comes with poor sleep. The poor sleep? That's been for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.59,
      "end_seconds": 77.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Have you had ankle swelling in the evenings?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.39,
      "end_seconds": 87.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "Well, yes, about the same, two months. With ankle swelling in the evenings, I'd say severe. There's breathlessness on slopes as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.08,
      "end_seconds": 89.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Alright, what about palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.01,
      "end_seconds": 91.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "No. No palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 91.61,
      "end_seconds": 95.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice palpitations. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.48,
      "end_seconds": 101.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.62,
      "end_seconds": 108.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. What about coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.87,
      "end_seconds": 112.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No coughing up blood, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.85,
      "end_seconds": 118.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fainting, black stools or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.22,
      "end_seconds": 123.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "No, no fainting, black stools or pain at rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.89,
      "end_seconds": 127.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Right. What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.25,
      "end_seconds": 129.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.3,
      "end_seconds": 132.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.14,
      "end_seconds": 138.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Uh, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.15,
      "end_seconds": 146.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Alright, moving on to your background, any past medical history? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.18,
      "end_seconds": 152.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Yeah, I have high blood pressure, for two years. Yes, diabetes. Yes, heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.1,
      "end_seconds": 170.34,
      "duration_seconds": 16.24,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Okay, diabetes, that's already on your record. Good to know. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.77,
      "end_seconds": 173.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Eggs. I come out in... well, stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.77,
      "end_seconds": 177.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Alright, are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.5,
      "end_seconds": 181.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Hmm, I'm on ramipril, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.44,
      "end_seconds": 184.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.11,
      "end_seconds": 191.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "It's, It's 5 milligrams. I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 192.27,
      "end_seconds": 196.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 4 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.96,
      "end_seconds": 201.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.59,
      "end_seconds": 209.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "No, uh, I left it at home. Clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.46,
      "end_seconds": 216.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.67,
      "end_seconds": 218.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.11,
      "end_seconds": 221.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.28,
      "end_seconds": 225.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.22,
      "end_seconds": 227.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.67,
      "end_seconds": 231.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.25,
      "end_seconds": 234.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.37,
      "end_seconds": 239.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.65,
      "end_seconds": 242.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.72,
      "end_seconds": 245.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "My father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 247.06,
      "end_seconds": 255.48,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. BP is 119 over 68, heart rate 82, temp 36.4 degrees, oxygen saturation is 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.54,
      "end_seconds": 262.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.36,
      "end_seconds": 265.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "It's, It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.87,
      "end_seconds": 269.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.09,
      "end_seconds": 271.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.48,
      "end_seconds": 275.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.86,
      "end_seconds": 292.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Chest is clear and heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.93,
      "end_seconds": 297.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.97,
      "end_seconds": 316.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "The scar on your chest has healed well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.33,
      "end_seconds": 347.22,
      "duration_seconds": 27.89,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like stable recovery after the heart event. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Medication side effects is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.7,
      "end_seconds": 351.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.52,
      "end_seconds": 369.56,
      "duration_seconds": 17.04,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now stable recovery after the heart event is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had occasional chest tightness for nearly five years, severe, and no black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.53,
      "end_seconds": 371.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.51,
      "end_seconds": 375.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "We should do a lipid profile for cardiovascular risk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 375.98,
      "end_seconds": 378.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "We've already done an ECG this morning, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.28,
      "end_seconds": 401.26,
      "duration_seconds": 21.98,
      "text": "Okay, thanks, I'll look at that. I'm prescribing atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. It's for cardiovascular risk. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Please don't stop the blood thinner on your own, even if you feel fine. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. We'll refer you to cardiac rehabilitation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.66,
      "end_seconds": 410.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.46,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 411.02,
      "end_seconds": 412.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.22,
      "end_seconds": 418.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.17,
      "end_seconds": 421.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.46,
      "end_seconds": 426.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Please come and see me in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.45,
      "end_seconds": 431.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 432.56,
      "end_seconds": 437.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.94,
      "end_seconds": 446.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "So, I take the atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.31,
      "end_seconds": 453.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 454.9,
      "end_seconds": 457.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "No, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}